  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Among following compounds, the number of those present in copper matte is</p><p>A.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CuCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>B.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math></p><p>C.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>D.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Copper Matte is a combination of copper sulphide and a small amount of iron sulphide. In the process of copper extraction, Matte is the stage after the final reduction process which involves converting it to crude copper.&nbsp;",
